course: dictionary
lesson: 2298
title: Crinkle: folds, faces and crackles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «A smile that crinkles the eyes usually means happy.» A smile changes the eyes, not the whole face in the same way, so crinkle must describe a small change around the eyes.
explain: «A real smile usually crinkles the skin around the eyes, not just the mouth.» Ask yourself what would fit in that gap. The skin around the eyes gets small folds or lines when someone really smiles, so to crinkle means to form many small folds or lines.
explain: Crinkle can also be a noun, meaning a small fold or line, and it can describe a soft crackling sound. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, your guess is probably right.
fact: Crinkle means to form many small folds or lines, or to make something do that.
fact: A crinkle is a small fold or line, like in paper or skin.
fact: To crinkle can mean to make a soft crackling sound, like a crisp packet.
fact: Crinkles is the he, she or it form of the verb, and crinkled is the past tense.
fact: Phrases to know: «crinkle your nose», «crinkle-cut chips», «crinkly paper».
exercise: «A real smile usually crinkles the skin around the eyes.» What does crinkles mean here? | *Forms small folds or lines | Makes a loud bang | Shines brightly | Falls off
exercise: Ella opens her crisp packet and it gives a soft crackle. What does crinkle mean in this sense? | To go sticky, like jam | To make a deep, low hum | To stay perfectly silent | *To make a soft crackling sound
exercise: Find and copy one word that means a small fold or line. | smile | frown | eyes | *crinkle
test: «A smile that crinkles the eyes usually means happy; a frown and tight lips may mean angry.» Which feeling does a crinkly-eyed smile show? | *Happy | Angry | Bored | Hungry
test: Grandma says, «Don't crinkle your nose like that, the milk has gone off.» What does crinkle your nose show? | Blowing your nose hard | *Wrinkling your nose because something smells bad | Holding your breath for a long time | Sneezing into a tissue
exam: «The foil ___ as Ali opened the wrapper.» Which word fits best in the gap? | froze | forgot | smiled | *crinkled
